        "content": "\n| Layer | Gap | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `web/` | No test runner in `package.json` — no vitest/jest devDependency, no config, no `test` script | You'll need to add one before any of the skeletons above can run. Recommend **Vitest** (fastest fit for a Next.js App Router + TS project, no Babel config needed) — **naming this per AGENTS.md's \"ask before adding a dependency\" rule, not installing it.** |\n| `engine/` | `pytest` is already a dev dependency but there's no `tests/` directory, no `conftest.py`, no `pytest.ini`/`[tool.pytest.ini_options]` in `pyproject.toml`, and no `pythonpath` config for the `agent`/`pipeline`/`connectors` imports (which are absolute, e.g. `from pipeline.schema import ...`) | Add `[tool.pytest.ini_options] pythonpath = [\".\"]` and a `tests/` tree mirroring the module tree, matching AGENTS.md's own `packages = [\"agent\", \"connectors\", \"eval\", \"pipeline\"]` list. |\n| both | No CI wiring runs either suite | Not yet applicable until a runner exists, but flagging so it isn't forgotten once one does. |\n\n",
